  "body": "Existing Development owner profiles include generated human REST queries, Admin UI proxy traffic, Admin-to-Gateway calls and native Dapr callbacks. Their actual receivers and callers must agree before a catalog cohort can activate or perform effects.\n\nBind installed SDK MVC actions, request/result schemas, effective policies, exact filters, loaded code and actual caller grants into an explicit schema-three/v2 composite. Peer calls verify the complete run binding and actual Dapr coordinates. Technical and native effects hold committed receiver leases; detached consistency work owns a separately admitted lifetime. Preserve actual UI/workload guards, issue the UI surface only at the owning Development issuers, and hand each selected state owner's private credential through its actual localhost transport while preserving the metadata response timeout.\n\nRequire explicit retained owner keys and private custody for persistent Development backends. Recomposition verifies the actual complete predecessor and backend; incomplete receipts or changed keys, backend, files or links preserve the prior valid custody. Selected-child preparation retains its actual launch/build mapping with bounded diagnostics and owned cleanup. Signed owner-query admission remains additional to ordinary public eligibility, including refusal of valid service signatures for UI-only operations. Existing finite-v1 absent-membership bytes and released constructor signatures remain intact.\n\nLocal verification of the frozen 133-file candidate on `484f4bd82fd2ef4b6c2653fdde57feeeb6d85a3c`:\n\n- AppHost custody, real model/renderer and selected-child preparation: 71/71; ServiceDefaults: 157/157; Contracts routing and historical goldens: 161/161, with no skips.\n- Full Server: 6,815 passes, no failures and 25 existing skips. Its owned listeners use explicit ephemeral URLs; unrelated running topology is untouched.\n- Unchanged secret scanner: 1/1 tracked and 1/1 complete-candidate; the actual index and all 133 source hashes remain unchanged.\n- Full DomainService: 1,299 passes, one missing declared Tenants source failure and one existing live-test skip. Earlier broad declared-source-governance failures remain retained, without weakening their guards or materializing nested checkouts.\n\nExact commands, environment, complete raw results and scanner/index-integrity receipts are retained in the qualification handoff. Standalone declared-source governance and actual selected owner cohort proof remain required before publication; local model/socket tests establish neither delivered packages nor runtime-image provenance.\n\nThe dated [release qualification audit](https://github.com/Hexalith/Hexalith.EventStore/blob/484f4bd82fd2ef4b6c2653fdde57feeeb6d85a3c/docs/operations/development-catalog-release-qualification.md) transparently records the initial direct push that bypassed PR/check rules and links its complete production comparison. That push is not represented as PR compliant. This candidate requires a separate normal current-base PR with every effective required context green, followed by normal squash merge, exact merged-source push proofs and protected publication. Owner releases, Builds/Platform pins and ordinary CLI/package proof remain separate completion gates.\n",
